recommend keep-going -- the next mechanical lap in this lane is the torus's third arm, the angle, which is the only one of the three still carrying no price. Degree and cut points now have numbers from two instruments each; the angle paper describes a quantity the sky computes and never subtracts, and nothing measures what that costs or buys. It wants its own round because the reading has to be built before it can be argued.
